+PhEntity {

  // Crest Factor. Ratio of a waveform's peak value to its RMS value. A clean
  // sine wave reads about 1.4; values that differ indicate waveform distortion
  // that can stress equipment.
  *elecCrestFactor: Marker

  // Even Total Harmonic Distortion (Even THD). THD computed from only the
  // even harmonics. Even harmonics can indicate asymmetry between the
  // positive and negative halves of a waveform, such as from half-wave
  // rectification or DC offset.
  *elecEvenThd: Marker

  // Order of the AC harmonic being measured, expressed as an integer
  // multiple of the fundamental frequency. For example on a 60Hz system an
  // order of 1 is the fundamental (60Hz), 3 is the third harmonic (180Hz),
  // and 5 is the fifth harmonic (300Hz).
  *elecHarmonicOrder: Int <minVal: 2>

  // Individual Harmonic Distortion (IHD). Magnitude of a single harmonic
  // as a percentage of the fundamental. Used to find which harmonic orders
  // dominate and to check them against per-order limits in standards such
  // as IEEE 519.
  *elecIhd: Marker

  // K-Factor. Weights harmonic currents by the square of their order to
  // estimate the added heating they cause in transformer windings. The
  // reading can be compared against a transformer's K-rating to check
  // whether it was designed to carry the load.
  *elecKFactor: Marker

  // Line 1 (L1) of an AC electric power system.
  *elecL1: Marker

  // Line 2 (L2) of an AC electric power system.
  *elecL2: Marker

  // Line 3 (L3) of an AC electric power system.
  *elecL3: Marker

  // Between line 1 (L1) and line 2 (L2) of an AC electric power system.
  *elecL1L2: Marker

  // Between line 2 (L2) and line 3 (L3) of an AC electric power system.
  *elecL2L3: Marker

  // Between line 3 (L3) and line 1 (L1) of an AC electric power system.
  *elecL3L1: Marker

  // Average of the L1, L2, and L3 values of a three-phase AC electric power
  // system, or the L1 and L2 values of an AC electric power system with two
  // lines.
  *elecLineAvg: Marker

  // Average of the L1-L2, L2-L3, and L3-L1 values of a three-phase AC
  // electric power system.
  *elecLineToLineAvg: Marker

  // Odd Total Harmonic Distortion (Odd THD). THD computed from only the odd
  // harmonics. These dominate in typical nonlinear loads such as drives and
  // rectifiers.
  *elecOddThd: Marker

  // Total Harmonic Distortion (THD). Combined magnitude of all harmonics as
  // a percentage of the fundamental. The primary overall indicator of
  // waveform distortion and power quality.
  *elecThd: Marker

  // Telephone Harmonic Form Factor (THFF). Ratio of the frequency weighted
  // components of a waveform to its RMS value. Estimates the potential for
  // interference with nearby communication circuits.
  *elecThff: Marker
}
